{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A Torah Moshe commanded us</b> — the reason one should always lift it up and say, 'A Torah Moshe commanded us,' and it shall be 'a heritage for the congregation of Jacob,' is that for all generations the children of Jacob shall inherit it and observe it, for it shall never be forgotten from the mouth of his seed. And our Rabbis expounded (Midrash Tehillim 1) that Scripture did not say 'heritage of the house of Jacob' or 'seed of Jacob,' but said <b>the congregation of Jacob</b>, to hint that many shall assemble upon them and the Torah shall forever be a heritage for Jacob and for all who assemble upon him — these are the converts who join themselves to YHWH to serve Him and are engrafted onto the house of Jacob, and all of them are called His congregation."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:41.392025041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}